  "items": [
    {
      "name": "It is not an infection",
      "char_file": "물방울_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "That lump is a tonsil stone, or",
        "tonsillolith, and it is not a sign",
        "that something is rotting",
        "",
        "It is compacted debris sitting in",
        "the natural pockets on the surface",
        "of your tonsils"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "What it is made of",
      "char_file": "물방울_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "A 2023 review describes them as",
        "calcified accumulations of food,",
        "cellular debris and microorganisms",
        "in the tonsillar crypts",
        "",
        "Stones smaller than 5 mm are",
        "common, larger ones are rare"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "How common is it?",
      "char_file": "물방울_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "A Japanese imaging study reviewed",
        "the CT scans of 2,873 patients and",
        "found tonsilloliths in 39.9%",
        "",
        "Mostly as incidental findings,",
        "peaking between 50 and 69"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Tongue first, then gargle",
      "char_file": "소금_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Clean the back of your tongue with",
        "a soft toothbrush, not just teeth,",
        "and floss daily",
        "",
        "Then gargle warm salt water,",
        "one teaspoon in a glass, after",
        "meals"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Stop your mouth drying out",
      "char_file": "물컵_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Saliva continuously rinses",
        "the tonsil crypts",
        "",
        "When it dries up overnight or",
        "during long stretches without",
        "drinking, bacteria get an",
        "easier run"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dehydration and smoking",
      "char_file": "담배_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Cleveland Clinic lists dehydration",
        "among the risk factors for",
        "tonsil stones",
        "",
        "It puts staying hydrated and",
        "quitting smoking on its",
        "prevention list"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Nothing sharp",
      "char_file": "손가락_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Do not go after a tonsil stone",
        "with anything sharp",
        "",
        "None of the national health",
        "services describe anything of",
        "the sort",
        "",
        "They usually fall out on their own,",
        "and antibiotics are not needed"
      ]
    }
  ],
